Phone number must start with + Phone number can only contain numbers after + Phone number is too short Phone number is too long
//fragments enter your phone number starting with the +(country code), then tap Login to proceed. You will receive a one-time use code via Telegram. Enter the code you received and tap Login to proceed. When you enable the (Remember Account) feature, the application will save your session and keep you logged in. However, to disconnect, you will need to manually log out by following the three steps outlined below. Please note: Any alerts about someone accessing your account are triggered by your login activity within the app. Your login credentials are never transmitted or stored outside your device, ensuring your account remains secure. Even if you choose not to enable the (Remember Account) feature, an unexpected or wrongful closure of the application may still result in your account remaining logged in. In such cases, you will need to manually log out to ensure your session is fully terminated. Additionally, you can delete all stored data by accessing the apps settings through the parameters menu (represented by the three dots icon) on the opening screen warning additional informations close STEP 1 STEP 2 STEP 3 to use the app, you have to disable the two-step verification To scan messages, enter a number between 100-100000. You can either choose manually or check your Telegram chat: 1) Open chat 2) Tap contact name 3) Select "Shared Media" 4) See total count. Scanning over 20000 messages may take longer. The app will automatically adjust if your number is too high.
//contact screen
select contact number of messages next Quantity must be more than 100 and less than 100000
